I followed the instructions set in the .DOCX:

Windows 11 host machine connected to an Ubuntu Server VM:

1) Created a VM with 4 gigs of RAM and 30 gb of space. Plenty for the project

2) Installed Ubuntu Server using official cannonical's ISO.

3) Configured two Network Adapters. The first one is NAT, it will allow access to internet. The second one is Host-Only,
   allowing me to connect to the server from Windows using SSH.

4) Created two accounts in the server, sysadmin and employee1. The former without sudo permissions.

5) Configured two static IP addresses for the internal Windows-Server network.
   192.168.50.1 for Windows, 192.168.50.20 for the Server.

6) Tested ping and SSH connections from Windows (see screenshots in the folder)

7) Wrote down this .MD to explain what i did.
